    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nSince 0977f70f4dd3 (#32549), `add_injection()` clips injection ranges to the parent's regions. But it checks for empty ranges **before** it clips them.\r\n\r\nIf a range lies fully outside the parent's regions, clipping turns it into an empty region. An empty region means \"whole buffer\". The child tree then parses the whole buffer, finds the same injection again, and repeats until the stack overflows.\r\n\r\nThis happens for both normal and combined injections. In real use, it shows up as 100% CPU and fast memory growth.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nClip the ranges first, then check for empty ranges. A range that clipping removes no longer creates a child tree.\r\n\r\nThe new test in `test/functional/treesitter/parser_spec.lua` uses the repro from the issue. It covers both normal and combined injections. It fails with `stack overflow` before the fix and passes after it.\r\n\r\nFixes #42477.",
